  "problem": "Which of the following is the graph of $y=\\sqrt{x}-2?$",
  "worked_solution": "To obtain the graph of $y=\\sqrt{x}-2,$ we can perform the following transformations:\n\n- Take the graph of $y=\\sqrt{x}.$\n\n- Translate the graph down by $2$ units to get the graph of $y=\\sqrt{x}-2.$\n\nThe result is the solid blue curve shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14238243/assets/b29dd00fae42bb810b95071e24ab395d9c5f9d3de967e6fa9541dcc0f93eaf80.png)",
